**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The relational keys a library version is queried and constrained by, written beside its row (001 §C 'Hybrid shape': facet keys and sample-version → material-version keys). In `LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`, two members on `LibraryEntryEnvelope`, both keyed by the content's `id` and `version` and both carrying step 62's `StorageBoundary` mark: (1) `member this.facetRows : Result<LibraryEntryFacetRow list, StorageError>`. The rows are the distinct attribute-key and discrete-value pairs of the existing facet catalogue (`LibraryFacets.fs`): `FacetKey` is the `AttributeKey`'s text, `FacetValue` the `DiscreteKey`'s text, and only `DiscreteValue`s are stored. A material's rows come from every `LibraryFacets.materialFacets []` attribute that applies to its decoded `MaterialEntry` (`toMaterialEntry`, step 25). A sample's, source's, polarizer's or detector's come from every `LibraryFacets.libraryFacets [] []` attribute that applies to its decoded `LibraryEntry` (`SampleItem`, `SourceItem`, `PolarizerItem`, `DetectorItem`). A category has none. Both catalogues are read over empty lists (step 46's signatures), so a row depends on its own entry alone. The material-category row's value is therefore the category's GUID text, which is what `CategoryId.categoryName []` answers (step 46), so renaming a category never stales a row. The facets a sample reads through its materials extract nothing, because the sample-material rows below hold that relation, and the numeric film-thickness facet is not stored. A decoder refusal is `LibraryRowInvalidErr` carrying its `describe` (step 39). (2) `member this.sampleMaterialRows : Result<LibrarySampleMaterialRow list, StorageError>`: for a sample, one row per element of its structure's `referencedMaterialVersions` (step 61), with `SampleId` and `SampleVersion` from the content and `MaterialId` and `MaterialVersion` from the reference; every other kind has none. No other key, index or derived column is added. (3) Tests, in `LibraryDatabaseTests`, over the envelopes of `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`: (a) `a material's facet rows hold its own discrete facets and key its category by id`: `MaterialIds.silicon`'s rows hold (`material-category`, the GUID text of `CategoryIds.semiconductor`), (`material-anisotropy`, `Isotropic`), (`material-dispersion`, `Dispersive`) and (`material-transparency`, `Absorbing`), and no `material-gyration-class`, `material-handedness` or `material-magnetic` row; `MaterialIds.langasite`'s hold (`material-anisotropy`, `Uniaxial`), (`material-gyration-class`, `Uniaxial 3 / 4 / 6 (g₁₁, g₃₃)`) and (`material-handedness`, `Right-handed`); and the `CategoryIds.glass` category entry has no row. (b) `an entry's facet rows are its kind and its own discrete facets`: `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` has exactly (`entry-kind`, `Sample`) and (`sample-has-thin-films`, `Has thin films`); `PresetIds.polarizerLp` exactly (`entry-kind`, `Polarizer`) and (`polarizer-category`, `Linear`); `PresetIds.source600` exactly (`entry-kind`, `Source`); and `PresetIds.detectorIntensity` exactly (`entry-kind`, `Detector`). (c) `a sample's material rows are every material version its structure references`: `SampleIds.langasiteSiliconId` has exactly the rows of `MaterialIds.langasite` and `MaterialIds.silicon` at version 1, `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` exactly those of `MaterialIds.glass152` and `MaterialIds.vacuumMaterial` at version 1, and `MaterialIds.silicon`'s material entry has none. (d) `every built-in's facet and material rows are stored beside its version row`: over `:memory:`, every envelope's version row (step 63, state `{ lifecycle = ActiveEntry; pin = VersionUnpinned }`), facet rows and sample-material rows are added in one `run` and saved; a second `run` reads back exactly the facet rows and the sample-material rows written; and deleting `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`'s version row also removes its facet and material rows (step 60's cascade).

**Acceptance.** After the keys land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a material's facet rows hold its own discrete facets and key its category by id`, `an entry's facet rows are its kind and its own discrete facets`, `a sample's material rows are every material version its structure references` and `every built-in's facet and material rows are stored beside its version row`; and build, elevation and the nine s08 invariants MUST pass.
